class_name Lore
extends RefCounted
## Where everything he fights with came from, a line each, as the cats tell it: read on a card with
## Tab, and at the smithy beside each thing. Weapons from the village's own past, things taken off
## the company, and the dodge mutations from the cats who taught them. Text only: what a thing does
## lives with the thing.

const STORIES := {
	"weapon:nunchaku": "The village once watched a kung fu film off a company generator. Nobody has been the same since.",
	"weapon:knife": "Every cat in the village carries one. Most of them use it on mangoes.",
	"weapon:keris": "A keris, her grandmother's, kept wrapped in cloth under the longhouse floor. The blade waves like a river.",
	"weapon:kerambit": "A kerambit, curved like a claw. The old ones say it was made by cats, for cats, and they may be right.",
	"weapon:handgun": "Dropped by a guard who ran. His name is still scratched into the grip.",
	"weapon:submachine_gun": "The same guard's, from his locker. He won't need it on the river road.",
	"weapon:machete": "Every farm has one. This one cleared paths, until the paths came for us.",
	"weapon:greatsword": "Two machetes' worth of steel, forged in one piece by a smith with something to prove.",
	"weapon:rifle": "Taken off a company truck, still in its crate, still oiled.",
	"weapon:automatic_rifle": "The rifle, with the smith's opinions added. Heavier, louder, and in no hurry to stop.",
	"weapon:assault_rifle": "Labeled \"security equipment\" on the shipping papers. Secure now.",
	"weapon:sniper_rifle": "The rifle, filed and fitted with a surveyor's scope. It measures giants now.",
	"weapon:shotgun": "The plantation guards used it on birds. The birds would like a word.",
	"weapon:grenade_launcher": "Listed as \"land clearing equipment\". It clears land.",
	"weapon:nail_gun": "Liberated from a company toolbox. The toolbox didn't complain.",
	"weapon:flare_gun": "Meant to call the helicopter in. It calls all sorts of things now.",
	"weapon:crossbow": "A hunter's bow on a stock, so even a kitten can hold it drawn.",
	"weapon:lamp_oil": "What lit the longhouse for a hundred nights. A bottle of it lights other things too.",
	"weapon:golok": "A golok: every kitchen has one, and every kitchen has opinions about it.",
	"weapon:celurit": "A celurit, the sickle for the rice harvest, and for whoever comes to burn the rice.",
	"weapon:hammer": "Uncle Anvil's. Tompel's keeping it for him, since he'd only put it down somewhere.",
	"weapon:rattan_staff": "Rattan bends and doesn't break. The Elder says that's the whole lesson.",
	"weapon:ketapel": "A ketapel: every kitten's first weapon, and every window's first enemy.",
	"weapon:sumpit": "A sumpit, from the Dayak cats upriver, who never miss and never brag about it.",
	"weapon:petasan": "Petasan, saved for the New Year. This year, the celebration comes early.",
	"weapon:tombak": "A tombak, like the ones the old guards held at the palace gates.",
	"weapon:bambu_runcing": "Bambu runcing: the grandparents' weapon in the war for independence. Bamboo remembers.",
	"weapon:mandau": "From the Dayak cats upriver, who call it a mandau. Its hilt is carved with hornbill feathers.",
	"weapon:rencong": "A rencong, from Aceh, its hilt shaped like a written prayer.",
	"weapon:badik": "A badik: a Bugis sailor's blade, carried for honor and drawn only when it must be.",
	"weapon:kujang": "A kujang, from the Sundanese west, shaped like the island it came from.",
	"weapon:panah": "A panah, a plain bow and arrows, the way his great-grandparents hunted.",
	"gear:vest": "A company safety vest with the bright strips cut off. Safety is for everyone now.",
	"gear:hard_hat": "It still says \"Safety First\". The company never said whose.",
	"gear:caping": "A caping, the woven farmer's hat. It keeps off the sun, the rain, and bad luck, they say.",
	"gear:bell_collar": "So the village always knows where he is. The rats hear it too, and worry.",
	"gear:scarf": "Red, so the others can find him in the smoke.",
	"gear:goggles": "From a welder's bench at the sawpits. The forest looks greener through them.",
	"gear:gloves": "Work gloves, four sizes too big, folded around his paws.",
	"gear:boots": "Kitten-sized boots, handed down six times, and still going.",
	"gear:jamu_flask": "Jamu: turmeric, ginger and something Auntie Clove won't name. Bitter. It works.",
	"gear:peci": "A peci, the black cap for Friday prayers. His grandfather's; it fits him now.",
	"gear:batik_shirt": "Dyed by the weaver, in a pattern only this village knows.",
	"gear:raincoat": "A company raincoat, cut down to size. It's been out in more rain than its owner ever was.",
	"gear:headlamp": "Off a surveyor's head. It lit up his maps of our forest; now it lights the way out.",
	"gear:sunglasses": "Left on a company dashboard. Darker than they need to be, like everything else in that truck.",
	"gear:bandana": "Tied the way the river cats tie theirs, the knot at the back.",
	"gear:wristbands": "Rubber bands off the company's permit folders. Thousands of permits, thousands of bands.",
	"gear:rubber_boots": "The plantation's boots, for wading through what it did to the peat.",
	"gear:sandals": "Light, loud, and the fastest thing in the village.",
	"gear:sarong": "Wrapped for the evening, tucked up for running.",
	"gear:tool_belt": "A surveyor's belt: every pocket full of the wrong tools, until the smith swapped them.",
	"gear:batik_headcloth": "A blangkon, folded tight, the knot at the back. The Elder's spare; he has opinions on how it sits.",
	"gear:ear_defenders": "Off a chainsaw worker's head. Quiet, at last.",
	"gear:life_jacket": "From the river road's ferry, in the company's orange. Floats. Also stops teeth.",
	"gear:kebaya": "A lace blouse, a kebaya, sewn by the weaver for the harvest festival. Nobody said it couldn't be worn to a fight.",
	"gear:lanyard": "A company badge on a lanyard. The guards wave him through for a second too long.",
	"gear:prayer_beads": "A tasbih, worn smooth by his grandfather's paws. Steadying.",
	"gear:safety_glasses": "Clear plastic, scratched, from the sawpits. Everything looks the same, but safer.",
	"gear:gem_rings": "Batu akik: rings of polished stone, the craze of a whole country one year. Lucky, says everyone selling one.",
	"gear:rattan_bracers": "Woven rattan around his forearms, the way the old fighters wore it.",
	"gear:wooden_clogs": "Bakiak, the clattering wooden clogs. Racing in pairs on one long pair is a festival game; kicking in them is not.",
	"gear:fighting_sash": "The sash of a silat school, tied by the teacher who said he'd never need it.",
	"support:gun_drone": "A survey drone that mapped our forest for the company. It has new loyalties.",
	"support:net_drone": "Built to net birds for the city markets. The nets catch rats now.",
	"support:layang_layang": "A fighting kite, its string coated in glass, the way the kites fought over the rice fields.",
	"support:meriam_bambu": "The bamboo cannon kittens fire at the end of the fasting month, loaded with stones.",
	"support:mines": "From the company's crates marked \"pest control\". The pests agree.",
	"support:ranjau_bambu": "Bamboo spikes, set the way the grandparents set them on jungle paths in the war.",
	"support:radio": "It plays the company's own jingle, loud. Their own dogs come running to it.",
	"support:bee_swarm": "Bees from the old hive under the longhouse. They know whose side they're on.",
	"support:alarm_drum": "The kentongan, the hollow bamboo drum that once called the village in from the fields.",
	"support:snare": "A jerat, a rattan loop the grandparents set for wild pigs. It works on boots.",
	"mutation:rolling_slash": "The Elder's lesson: never just get out of the way. Roll through, blade out.",
	"mutation:land_on_feet": "The Elder's first lesson: a cat lands on his feet, and gets up rolling.",
	"mutation:pounce": "How Granny Whiskers hunted when she was young: over the crowd, onto the one that matters.",
	"mutation:riposte": "Granny Whiskers again: \"Let them swing first. Be there after.\"",
	"mutation:ankle_cutter": "Patch learned it in the sawpits: a giant's boots are slow to turn.",
	"mutation:long_leap": "Saffron never uses the bridge over the stream. She showed you why.",
	"mutation:more_charges": "Keep up with Coffee and Cream for a week, and you won't sit still either.",
	"mutation:lick_your_wounds": "Auntie Clove's first rule: \"Tend to it as you go. You'll have time to fuss later.\"",
	"mutation:caltrops": "Patch filled his pockets with the sawpits' bent nails. \"Drop them as you go. Boots hate them.\"",
	"mutation:slipstream": "Coffee and Cream run in each other's wake, and arrive everywhere first.",
	"mutation:dust_cloud": "Saffron kicks up the clearing's dust and is gone before it settles.",
	"mutation:scent_trail": "Auntie Clove's turmeric: the company's dogs will follow it anywhere, and that's the point.",
	"mutation:chain_roll": "Skipper never stops a roll halfway: \"Finish one, start the next.\"",
}


## The story of a thing, by its kind ("weapon", "gear", "support" or "mutation") and id, or "".
static func of(kind: String, id: String) -> String:
	return STORIES.get(kind + ":" + id, "")
